`cython_library()` builds each Cython extension as a `cc_binary` with
`linkshared = 1` that deliberately leaves every `Py*` symbol
undefined, to be resolved by the interpreter that loads it. On MacOS
that only links if `-undefined dynamic_lookup` is passed.

Bazel 6's MacOS crosstool added that flag to every
`cpp_link_dynamic_library` / `cpp_link_nodeps_dynamic_library` action
from its `default_link_flags` feature. Bazel 8's does not, so linking
`cygrpc.so` fails with several hundred `Undefined symbols for
architecture arm64` errors.

Passing the flag through `--linkopt` in our `.bazelrc` would apply it
to every MacOS link, including executables, where it would turn a
genuine missing-symbol error into a crash at run time. Setting it on
the one target that wants it keeps that error checking everywhere
else.
diff -ru grpc-1.71.0.orig/bazel/cython_library.bzl grpc-1.71.0/bazel/cython_library.bzl
--- grpc-1.71.0.orig/bazel/cython_library.bzl
+++ grpc-1.71.0/bazel/cython_library.bzl
@@ -75,6 +75,10 @@
             deps = deps + ["@local_config_python//:python_headers"],
             defines = defines,
             linkshared = 1,
+            linkopts = select({
+                "@platforms//os:macos": ["-Wl,-undefined,dynamic_lookup"],
+                "//conditions:default": [],
+            }),
         )
         shared_objects.append(shared_object_name)

